# postinst/prerm/postrm call `systemctl daemon-reload`, `try-restart` and
# `stop` of the headless unit only -- never enable, start, or mask any unit (see those scripts' own header comments:
# this package deliberately never auto-enables the per-user daemon unit).
# `daemon-reload` is the safe, policy-compliant case this tag's real
# violations (enabling/starting without a trigger, bypassing debhelper's
# unit lifecycle) don't cover -- not something to restructure around.
yadorilink: maintainer-script-calls-systemctl
